{'symbol': 'ABMD', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Abiomed, Inc. Presents at Piper Jaffray 31st Annual Healthcare Conference, Dec-04-2019 03:00 PM', 'text': 'Abiomed, Inc. Presents at Piper Jaffray 31st Annual Healthcare Conference, Dec-04-2019 03:00 PM. Venue: The Lotte New York Palace, 455 Madison Avenue, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Michael R. Minogue, Chairman, CEO & President.'}{'symbol': 'ACN', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Accenture and Snam Sign a Memorandum of Understanding to Study and Assess Solutions Based on Internet of Things (IoT) Technologies', 'text': 'Accenture and Snam have signed a memorandum of understanding to study and assess solutions based on Internet of Things (IOT) technologies to boost innovation and sustainability of energy networks as part of the global strategic push towards an energy transition. The collaboration is part of a broad initiative by Snam - dubbed "SnamTec, Tomorrow’s Energy Company" - that calls for investments of over €1.4 billion in innovation and energy transition by 2023 involving everything from the application of new technologies to increase the networks’ sustainability to a commitment to green sectors such as sustainable mobility, renewable gas, hydrogen and energy efficiency. Accenture and Snam will research and assess solutions for internet-connected devices and other technologies - such as machine learning and artificial intelligence, edge and fog computing and advanced analytics - to optimize the monitoring and maintenance of infrastructure to make it smarter and more sustainable, generating a positive impact on surrounding regions and communities. Another objective of the collaboration will be to carry out analyses on the growing role of renewable gases such as biomethane and hydrogen on the energy mix of the future.'}{'symbol': 'ALGN', 'date': '2019-11-27 14:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'U.S. ITC Affirms ALJ Finding That 3Shape Infringes 3 Align Technology Patents But Declines To Find Section 337 Violation', 'text': "ALIGN TECHNOLOGY - INTERNATIONAL TRADE COMMISSION AFFIRMS ALJ FINDING 3SHAPE INFRINGES 3 OF CO'S PATENTS BUT DECLINES TO FIND SECTION 337 VIOLATION.ALIGN TECHNOLOGY - CO REVIEWING U.S. ITC DECISION TO DECLINE TO FIND A VIOLATION OF SECTION 337 AND WILL CONSIDER APPROPRIATE RESPONSE."}{'symbol': 'ABC', 'date': '2019-11-27 16:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Federal Prosecutors Launch Criminal Probe Of Opioid Makers, Distributors - WSJ', 'text': ':FEDERAL PROSECUTORS LAUNCH CRIMINAL PROBE OF OPIOID MAKERS, DISTRIBUTORS'}{'symbol': 'AON', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Aon plc has filed a Shelf Registration in the amount of $1.01615 billion.', 'text': 'Aon plc has filed a Shelf Registration in the amount of $1.01615 billion.\n\nSecurity Name: Class A Ordinary Shares\nSecurities Offered: 5,000,000\nTransaction Features: ESOP Related Offering'}{'symbol': 'AJG', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Arthur J. Gallagher & Co. (NYSE:AJG) agreed heads of terms to acquire additional 80% stake in Capsicum Reinsurance Brokers LLP.', 'text': 'Arthur J. Gallagher & Co. (NYSE:AJG) agreed heads of terms to acquire additional 80% stake in Capsicum Reinsurance Brokers LLP on November 27, 2019. Post acquisition, Arthur J. Gallagher & Co. will own 100% in Capsicum Re. The deal remains subject to necessary regulatory approvals and the execution of relevant agreements.\n'}{'symbol': 'ADSK', 'date': '2019-11-27 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Autodesk Inc Reports Q3 Non-Gaap Earnings Per Share $0.78', 'text': 'AUTODESK, INC. ANNOUNCES FISCAL 2020 THIRD QUARTER RESULTS.Q3 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.78.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.30.Q3 REVENUE $843 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $825.8 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.72 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY TOTAL ARR INCREASED 28 PERCENT TO $3.22 BILLION.QTRLY TOTAL BILLINGS INCREASED 55 PERCENT TO $1.01 BILLION.QTRLY TOTAL ARR WAS $3.22 BILLION, AN INCREASE OF 28 PERCENT AS REPORTED, AND ON A CONSTANT CURRENCY BASIS.QTRLY SUBSCRIPTION PLAN ARR WAS $2.86 BILLION, AN INCREASE OF 49 PERCENT AS REPORTED, AND 50 PERCENT ON A CONSTANT CURRENCY BASIS.QTRLY CORE ARR INCREASED 23 PERCENT TO $2.99 BILLION.SEES 2020 TOTAL ARR $3,405 MILLION - $3,445 MILLION.SEES 2020 REVENUE OF $3,255 MILLION - $3,270 MILLION.SEES 2020 BILLINGS OF $4,050 MILLION - $4,090 MILLION.SEES 2020 GAAP EPS $0.80 - $0.85.SEES 2020 NON-GAAP EPS $2.74 - $2.79.SEES 2020 FREE CASH FLOW OF $1,300 MILLION - $1,340 MILLION.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.75, REVENUE VIEW $3.26 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'BAC', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Bank of America Corporation has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $4.725 million.', 'text': 'Bank of America Corporation has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $4.725 million.\n\nSecurity Name: Floating Rate Senior Unsecured Notes due December 1, 2059\nSecurity Type: Corporate Bond/Note (Non Convertible)\nPrincipal Amount: $4.725 million\nPrice\\Range: 100%\nDiscount Per Security: 1%\nSecurity Features: Floating Rate; MTN; Puttable\nCoupon Type: Variable\n'}{'symbol': 'BBY', 'date': '2019-11-27 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Best Buy Sets Regular Quarterly Cash Dividend Of $0.50 Per Share', 'text': 'SETS REGULAR QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND OF $0.50PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'BBY', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Best Buy Co., Inc. Announces Regular Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on January 7, 2020', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Best Buy Co., Inc. has authorized the payment of a regular quarterly cash dividend of $0.50 per common share. The quarterly dividend is payable on January 7, 2020, to shareholders of record as of the close of business on December 17, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'BKNG', 'date': '2019-11-27 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Booking Holdings To Transfer Listing Of Debt Securities To Nasdaq', 'text': 'BOOKING HOLDINGS TO TRANSFER LISTING OF DEBT SECURITIES TO NASDAQ.BOOKING HOLDINGS -  WILL BE TRANSFERRING SECURITIES EXCHANGE LISTING FOR CERTAIN NOTES FROM NYSE TO CORPORATE BOND EXCHANGE OF NASDAQ STOCK MARKET LLC.BOOKING HOLDINGS INC - NOTES ARE EXPECTED TO BEGIN TRADING AS NASDAQ-LISTED SECURITIES ON DECEMBER 9, 2019.BOOKING HOLDINGS INC -  TO TRANSFER LISTING OF DEBT SECURITIES TO NASDAQ, EFFECTIVE DECEMBER 6, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'CNC', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Quartet Health, Inc. announced that it has received $67.5 million in funding from a group of investors', 'text': 'On November 27, 2019, Quartet Health, Inc. closed the transaction. The company amended the terms of the transaction. The company received $67,500,000 in the transaction. The company has raised $7,500,000 in its second tranche. The transaction included participation from returning investor Deerfield Management Company, L.P. along with Echo Health Ventures. The company has raised $160,500,000 in funding till date.'}{'symbol': 'SCHW', 'date': '2019-11-27 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Fitch Ratings Says Schwab's 'A'/'F1' Ratings Unaffected By Proposed TD Ameritrade Acquisition", 'text': "FITCH RATINGS SAYS SCHWAB'S 'A'/'F1' RATINGS UNAFFECTED BY PROPOSED TD AMERITRADE ACQUISITION.FITCH SAYS VIEWS STRATEGIC RATIONALE AND POTENTIAL COST SYNERGIES OF PROPOSED TD AMERITRADE-CHARLES SCHWAB MERGER FAVORABLY.FITCH SAYS LONGER-TERM, IT BELIEVES POTENTIAL BENEFITS FROM TD AMERITRADE-CHARLES SCHWAB DEAL, IF EXECUTED WELL, COULD OUTWEIGH DOWNSIDE RISKS.FITCH- THERE IS A POSSIBILITY THAT PROPOSED TD AMERITRADE-CHARLES SCHWAB MERGER COULD DRAW ANTITRUST SCRUTINY."}{'symbol': 'CTXS', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Citrix Systems, Inc. Enters into an Amended and Restated Credit Agreement with Bank of America, N.A', 'text': "On November 26, 2019, Citrix Systems, Inc. (the 'Company') entered into an amended and restated credit agreement (the 'Credit Agreement') with Bank of America, N.A., as administrative agent, and the other lenders party thereto from time to time (collectively, the 'Lenders'), which amends and restates the Company’s Credit Agreement, dated as of January 7, 2015. The Credit Agreement provides for a $250 million unsecured revolving credit facility for a term of five years. The Company may elect to increase the revolving credit facility by up to $250 million if existing or new lenders provide additional revolving commitments in accordance with the terms of the Credit Agreement. The proceeds of borrowings under the Credit Agreement may be used for working capital and general corporate purposes. Borrowings under the Credit Agreement will bear interest at a rate equal to (a) either (i) a customary London interbank offered rate formula (“LIBOR”) or, upon a phase-out of LIBOR, an alternative benchmark rate as provided in the Credit Agreement, or (ii) a customary base rate formula, plus (b) the applicable margin with respect thereto, which initially will be determined based on the Company’s consolidated leverage ratio but may, if so elected by the Company, be based on the Company’s non-credit enhanced, senior unsecured long-term debt rating as determined by Moody’s Investors Service, Inc., Standard & Poor’s Financial Services, LLC and Fitch Ratings Inc., in each case as set forth in the Credit Agreement."}{'symbol': 'COST', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Costco Wholesale Corporation Announces Not Stand for Re-Election of John W. Meisenbach as Member of the Board', 'text': 'On November 25, 2019, John W. Meisenbach, who has been a member of the Board of Directors of Costco Wholesale Corporation for over thirty-six years, submitted a letter stating that he will not be standing for re-election as member of the Board when his current term expires, effective on commencement of the Company’s 2020 annual meeting.'}{'symbol': 'DE', 'date': '2019-11-27 14:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Deere Says First Phase Of Early Orders For Combines Are Down Double-Digits- Conf Call', 'text': "DEERE SAYS FIRST PHASE OF EARLY ORDERS FOR COMBINES WERE DOWN DOUBLE-DIGITS- CONF CALL.DEERE SAYS EARLY ORDERS FOR PLANTERS WERE UP SINGLE DIGITS- CONF CALL.DEERE SAYS EARLY ORDERS FOR SPRAYERS WERE DOWN LOW DOUBLE-DIGITS.DEERE SAYS UNCERTAINTY HAS SLOWED REPLACEMENT EQUIPMENT DEMAND IN 2019.DEERE SAYS SEEING SOME EVIDENCE THAT U.S. FARMER SENTIMENT IS BEGINNING TO IMPROVE.DEERE SAYS FLEET AGE IN THE U.S. HAS REACHED ITS HIGHEST POINT IN OVER A DECADE, AND CO'S 2020 OUTLOOK ANTICIPATES EVEN FURTHER AGING OF THIS FLEET.DEERE SAYS MANY U.S. CUSTOMERS WILL REACH A POINT  IN 2020 WHERE THEY SIMPLY NEED TO REPLACE THEIR EQUIPMENT.DEERE SAYS TRACTOR ORDER BOOK CURRENTLY EXTENDS THROUGH THE END OF MARCH, WELL AHEAD OF LAST YEAR.DEERE SAYS LEASE RETURN RATES REMAIN AT ELEVATED LEVELS.DEERE SAYS HAS TAKEN ACTIONS TO REDUCE CO'S MATURED LEASE INVENTORY.DEERE SAYS ANNOUNCED $140 MILLION VOLUNTARY SEPARATION PROGRAM FOR SALARIED EMPLOYEES.DEERE SAYS WILL REVIEW OVERSEAS FOOTPRINT.DEERE SAYS VOLUNTARY SEPARATION PROGRAM, COMBINED WITH INITIATIVES TAKEN IN 2019, IS ESTIMATED TO CONTRIBUTE TO ANNUALIZED SAVINGS OF ABOUT $150 MILLION.DEERE SAYS VOLUNTARY SEPARATION COSTS WILL BE INCURRED IN THE FIRST QUARTER OF FISCAL 2020."}{'symbol': 'DE', 'date': '2019-11-27 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Deere & Co Posts Qtrly Earnings Per Share Of $2.27', 'text': 'QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.27.QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.14.FULL-YEAR 2020 FORECAST CALLS FOR NET INCOME OF $2.7 TO $3.1 BILLION, REFLECTING UNCERTAINTIES IN OUR EQUIPMENT OPERATIONS..WORLDWIDE NET SALES AND REVENUES INCREASED 5 PERCENT IN FOURTH QUARTER TO $9.896 BILLION."JOHN DEERE’S PERFORMANCE REFLECTED CONTINUED UNCERTAINTIES IN THE AGRICULTURAL SECTOR".Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.13, REVENUE VIEW $8.53 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.NET INCOME IN Q4 WAS FAVORABLY AFFECTED BY DISCRETE ADJUSTMENTS TO PROVISION FOR INCOME TAXES.ADJUSTMENTS RELATED TO TAX REFORM WERE $41 MILLION IN Q4.DEERE- TRADE TENSIONS, DIFFICULT GROWING, HARVESTING CONDITIONS CAUSED MANY FARMERS TO BECOME CAUTIOUS ABOUT MAKING MAJOR INVESTMENTS IN NEW EQUIPMENT.WORLDWIDE SALES OF AGRICULTURE AND TURF EQUIPMENT ARE FORECAST TO DECLINE 5 TO 10 PERCENT FOR FISCAL-YEAR 2020.WORLDWIDE SALES OF CONSTRUCTION AND FORESTRY EQUIPMENT ARE ANTICIPATED TO BE DOWN 10 TO 15 PERCENT FOR 2020.DEERE - FAVOURABLE GENERAL ECONOMIC CONDITIONS SUPPORTED DEMAND FOR SMALLER EQUIPMENT, LED TO "SOLID RESULTS" FOR CONSTRUCTION AND FORESTRY BUSINESS.DEERE - DESPITE PRESENT CHALLENGES, THE LONGER-TERM OUTLOOK FOR OUR BUSINESSES REMAINS HEALTHY.AGRICULTURE & TURF NET SALES OF $5,756 MILLION , UP 3% IN QUARTER.DEERE’S WORLDWIDE SALES OF AGRICULTURE AND TURF EQUIPMENT ARE FORECAST TO DECLINE 5% TO 10% FOR FISCAL-YEAR 2020.'}{'symbol': 'DE', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Deere & Company Provides Earnings Forecast for the Full Year 2020', 'text': 'Deere & Company provided earnings forecast for the full year 2020. Net income attributable to Deere & Company for fiscal 2020 is forecast to be in a range of $2.7 billion to $3.1 billion.'}{'symbol': 'EMN', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Eastman Chemical Company Presents at Citigroup’s 2019 Basic Materials Conference 2019, Dec-03-2019 10:15 AM', 'text': 'Eastman Chemical Company Presents at Citigroup’s 2019 Basic Materials Conference 2019, Dec-03-2019 10:15 AM. Venue: The Wagner at the Battery, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Curtis E. Espeland, Executive VP & CFO.'}{'symbol': 'ECL', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ecolab Inc. Presents at Citigroup’s 2019 Basic Materials Conference 2019, Dec-03-2019 10:15 AM', 'text': 'Ecolab Inc. Presents at Citigroup’s 2019 Basic Materials Conference 2019, Dec-03-2019 10:15 AM. Venue: The Wagner at the Battery, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Darrell R. Brown, Executive VP & President of the Global Industrial Sector.'}{'symbol': 'EMR', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Emerson Electric Co. Solicits Proxies from the Shareholders', 'text': 'On November 27, 2019, Emerson Electric Co. filed a preliminary proxy statement and urged the shareholders of the Company to vote for the Company’s nominees in the upcoming annual meeting of shareholders to be held on February 4, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'XOM', 'date': '2019-11-27 15:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Exxon Reports Leak at Beaumont, TX. Refinery; Expects Some Impact to Production', 'text': 'REPORTS LEAK ON A PIPE RESULTED IN MATERIAL RELEASE AT BEAUMONT, TEXAS, REFINERY .REPORTS EMISSIONS FROM CRUDE UNIT B 05FUG_001 AT BEAUMONT, TEXAS REFINERY .REPORTS REFINERY ANTICIPATES SOME IMPACT TO PRODUCTION.'}{'symbol': 'FB', 'date': '2019-11-27 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Oculus Says Announcing Acquisition Of Beat Games', 'text': "OCULUS SAYS ANNOUNCING ACQUISITION OF BEAT GAMES.OCULUS SAYS BEAT GAMES WILL JOIN CO'S STUDIOS AS AN INDEPENDENTLY OPERATED STUDIO IN PRAGUE."}{'symbol': 'FE', 'date': '2019-11-27 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Firstenergy Entered Into Amendment To Settlement Agreement With Ad HOC Noteholders Group, Bruce Mansfield Certificateholders Group', 'text': 'FIRSTENERGY - ENTERED INTO AMENDMENT TO SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT WITH AD HOC NOTEHOLDERS GROUP, BRUCE MANSFIELD CERTIFICATEHOLDERS GROUP.FIRSTENERGY CORP - ALSO ENTERED INTO AMENDMENT TO SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT WITH OFFICIAL COMMITTEE OF UNSECURED CREDITORS.'}{'symbol': 'GM', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'General Motors Names Ral Mier as New Director of Sales and Operations for Colombia', 'text': 'General Motors has named Ral Mier as its new director of sales and operations for Colombia. The move is part of the manufacturers consolidation of its South American business and follows the merge of its three branches in the region earlier this year. Mier has worked in the automotive sector for more than 20 years in roles such as marketing, planning, exports and financing. His previous posts have included Chile and Japan and he holds an undergraduate degree from the Universidad de los Andes with postgraduate studies in international business and negotiation strategies.'}{'symbol': 'GM', 'date': '2019-11-27 16:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cox Automotive Says Annual Vehicle Sales Pace In November Is Forecast To Finish Near 16.9 Mln', 'text': 'COX AUTOMOTIVE - ANNUAL VEHICLE SALES PACE IN NOVEMBER IS FORECAST TO FINISH NEAR 16.9 MILLION, UP FROM OCTOBER\'S 16.5 MILLION LEVEL.COX AUTOMOTIVE - NOVEMBER SALES VOLUME IS EXPECTED TO FALL SLIGHTLY TO 1.39 MILLION, DOWN 0.4% OR ABOUT 5,000 UNITS FROM NOVEMBER 2018.COX AUTOMOTIVE SAYS "A NEW SALES RECORD FOR NOVEMBER IS POSSIBLE DUE TO AN ADDITIONAL SELLING DAY AND UPSIDE POTENTIAL OF FLEET SALES".COX AUTOMOTIVE - TOTAL SALES THROUGH OCTOBER 2019 ARE DOWN 1.4% COMPARED TO LAST YEAR, AND NEGATIVE TREND IS EXPECTED TO CONTINUE.COX AUTOMOTIVE- IN NOV., NEW LIGHT-VEHICLE SALES, INCLUDING FLEET, ARE FORECAST TO REACH 1.39 MILLION UNITS, DOWN ABOUT 5,000 UNITS OR 0.4% VERSUS NOV. 2018.COX AUTOMOTIVE SAYS "ANOTHER KEY FACTOR FOR NOVEMBER\'S RESULTS WILL BE THE RECOVERY OF GM SALES IN THE WAKE OF THE LONG" GM-UAW STRIKE.'}{'symbol': 'HSIC', 'date': '2019-11-27 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Henry Schein Says On Nov. 20, Co Committed To Contemplated Initiative Previously Disclosed In Its Nov. 5 Earnings Release', 'text': 'HENRY SCHEIN SAYS ON NOV. 20, CO COMMITTED TO CONTEMPLATED INITIATIVE PREVIOUSLY DISCLOSED IN ITS NOV. 5 EARNINGS RELEASE - SEC FILING.HENRY SCHEIN - UNABLE TO MAKE DETERMINATION OF ESTIMATE OF AMOUNT EXPECTED TO BE INCURRED IN CONNECTION WITH NOV. 5 DISCLOSED CONTEMPLATED INITIATIVE.'}{'symbol': 'HOLX', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hologic, Inc. Presents at Piper Jaffray 31st Annual Healthcare Conference, Dec-04-2019 09:00 AM', 'text': 'Hologic, Inc. Presents at Piper Jaffray 31st Annual Healthcare Conference, Dec-04-2019 09:00 AM. Venue: The Lotte New York Palace, 455 Madison Avenue, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Karleen Oberton, CFO, Michael J. Watts, Vice President of Investor Relations & Corporate Communications.'}{'symbol': 'HPQ', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Xerox Holdings Provides Information to Shareholders', 'text': 'On November 27, 2019, Xerox Holdings Corporation announced that it would address its bid straight to the shareholders of HP Inc. after the Company rejected its due diligence request. Xerox stated that it had previously given the Company a November 25 deadline to agree on friendly discussions as well as on mutual due diligence and it did not disclose further details about its next moves and there are various possible options, including a hostile tender offer or a proxy fight. Xerox stated that it also reiterated the benefits from a deal and again refuted the Company’s claims that its proposal was ‘highly conditional’ and ‘uncertain’, also highlighting that there would be no financing condition to the completion of the acquisition.'}{'symbol': 'HPQ', 'date': '2019-11-27 21:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hp Inc Reports Q4 Non-Gaap Earnings Per Share $0.60', 'text': '. REPORTS FISCAL 2019 FULL YEAR AND FOURTH QUARTER RESULTS.Q4 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.60.Q4 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.26.Q4 REVENUE $15.4 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $15.25 BILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.58 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FOR FISCAL 2020 Q1, ESTIMATES GAAP DILUTED NET EPS TO BE IN RANGE OF $0.39 TO $0.42 & NON-GAAP DILUTED NET EPS TO BE IN RANGE OF $0.53 TO $0.56.FISCAL 2020 Q1 NON-GAAP DILUTED NET EPS ESTIMATES EXCLUDE $0.14 PER DILUTED SHARE, PRIMARILY RELATED TO RESTRUCTURING & OTHER CHARGES.QTRLY PERSONAL SYSTEMS NET REVENUE $10.43 BILLION VERSUS $10.06 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.FOR FISCAL 2020, ESTIMATES GAAP DILUTED NET EPS TO BE IN RANGE OF $2.00 TO $2.10 & NON-GAAP DILUTED NET EPS TO BE IN RANGE OF $2.24 TO $2.32.FISCAL 2020 NON-GAAP DILUTED NET EPS ESTIMATES EXCLUDE $0.22 TO $0.24 PER DILUTED SHARE, PRIMARILY RELATED TO RESTRUCTURING & OTHER CHARGES.QTRLY PRINTING NET REVENUE $4.98 BILLION VERSUS $5.3 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.53 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.23 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q4 NON-GAAP NET EARNINGS & NON-GAAP DILUTED NET EPS EXCLUDE AFTER-TAX ADJUSTMENTS OF $511 MILLION, OR $0.34 PER DILUTED SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'HPQ', 'date': '2019-11-27 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'HP Inc Says Expects Industry-Wide CPU Supply Constraints To Persist Through First Half Of 2020 - Conf Call', 'text': 'HP INC SAYS FOR 2020, EXPECT MACROECONOMIC CONDITIONS TO REMAIN DYNAMIC, AS THEY ARE TODAY, AND EXPECT END MARKETS TO REMAIN COMPETITIVE - CONF CALL.HP INC SAYS IN PRINTING BUSINESS, CO IS ASSUMING A YEAR-OVER-YEAR UNIT MARKET DECLINE, DRIVEN BY THE HOME MARKET - CONF CALL.HP INC SAYS EXPECTS INDUSTRY-WIDE CPU SUPPLY CONSTRAINTS TO PERSIST THROUGH FIRST HALF OF 2020 - CONF CALL.HP INC EXEC SAYS EXPECTS LARGER REVENUE IMPACT OF CPU SUPPLY CONSTRAINTS IN Q1 2020 THAN IN Q4 - CONF CALL.'}{'symbol': 'INCY', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Incyte Corporation Announces Acceptance and Priority Review of NDA for Pemigatinib as a Treatment for Patients with Cholangiocarcinoma', 'text': 'Incyte announced that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has accepted for Priority Review its New Drug Application (NDA) for pemigatinib, a selective fibroblast growth factor receptor (FGFR) inhibitor, as a treatment for patients with previously treated, locally advanced or metastatic cholangiocarcinoma with FGFR2 fusions or rearrangements. The NDA submission is based on data from the FIGHT-202 study evaluating pemigatinib as a treatment for patients with previously treated, locally advanced or metastatic cholangiocarcinoma. Study results, recently presented at the European Society for Medical Oncology (ESMO) 2019 Congress, demonstrated that in patients harboring FGFR2 fusions or rearrangements (Cohort A), pemigatinib monotherapy resulted in an overall response rate (ORR) of 36% (primary endpoint), and median duration of response (DOR) of 7.5 months (secondary endpoint) with a median follow-up of 15 months. Adverse events were manageable and consistent with the mechanism of action of pemigatinib. The FDA grants Priority Review to medicines that may offer a major advance in treatment where none currently exists. This designation shortens the review period to eight months compared to 12 months for Standard Review. The Prescription Drug User Fee Act (PDUFA) target action date is May 30, 2020. Cholangiocarcinoma is a rare cancer that forms in the bile duct. It is classified based on its origin: intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma (iCCA) occurs in the bile duct inside the liver and extrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma occurs in the bile duct outside the liver. Patients with cholangiocarcinoma are often diagnosed at a late or advanced stage when the prognosis is poor. The incidence of cholangiocarcinoma varies regionally and ranges between 0.3 – 3.4 per 100,000 in North America and Europe.1 FGFR2 fusions or rearrangements occur almost exclusively in iCCA, where they are observed in 10-16% of patients. The FIGHT-202 Phase 2, open-label, multicenter study (NCT02924376) is evaluating the safety and efficacy of pemigatinib – a selective fibroblast growth factor receptor (FGFR) inhibitor – in adult (age = 18 years) patients with previously treated, locally advanced or metastatic cholangiocarcinoma with documented FGF/FGFR status. Patients were enrolled into one of three cohorts – Cohort A (FGFR2 fusions or rearrangements), Cohort B (other FGF/FGFR genetic alterations) or Cohort C (no FGF/FGFR genetic alterations). All patients received 13.5 mg pemigatinib orally once daily (QD) on a 21-day cycle (two weeks on/one week off) until radiological disease progression or unacceptable toxicity. The primary endpoint of FIGHT-202 is overall response rate (ORR) in Cohort A, assessed by independent review per RECIST v1.1. Secondary endpoints include ORR in Cohorts B, A plus B, and C; progression free survival (PFS), overall survival (OS), duration of response (DOR), disease control rate (DCR) and safety in all cohorts. The FIGHT (FIbroblast Growth factor receptor in oncology and Hematology Trials) clinical trial program includes ongoing Phase 2 and 3 studies investigating safety and efficacy of pemigatinib therapy across several FGFR-driven malignancies. Phase 2 monotherapy studies include FIGHT-202, as well as FIGHT-201 investigating pemigatinib in patients with metastatic or surgically unresectable bladder cancer, including with activating FGFR3 mutations or fusions/rearrangements; FIGHT-203 in patients with myeloproliferative neoplasms with activating FGFR1 fusions/rearrangements; FIGHT-207 in patients with previously treated, locally-advanced/metastatic or surgically unresectable solid tumor malignancies harboring activating FGFR mutations or fusions/rearrangements, irrespective of tumor type. FIGHT-205 is a Phase 2 study investigating pemigatinib plus pembrolizumab combination therapy and pemigatinib monotherapy in patients with previously untreated, metastatic or unresectable bladder cancer harboring FGFR3 mutations or fusions/rearrangements who are not eligible to receive cisplatin. FIGHT-302 is a recently initiated Phase 3 study investigating pemigatinib as a first-line treatment for patients with cholangiocarcinoma with FGFR2 fusions or rearrangements. Fibroblast growth factor receptors (FGFRs) play an important role in tumor cell proliferation and survival, migration and angiogenesis (the formation of new blood vessels). Activating fusions, rearrangements, translocations and gene amplifications in FGFRs are closely correlated with the development of various cancers. Pemigatinib is a potent, selective, oral inhibitor of FGFR isoforms 1, 2 and 3 which, in preclinical studies, has demonstrated selective pharmacologic activity against cancer cells with FGFR alterations. The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has granted pemigatinib Breakthrough Therapy designation for the treatment of previously treated, advanced/metastatic or unresectable FGFR2 translocated cholangiocarcinoma. The FDA’s Breakthrough Therapy designation is designed to expedite the development and review of drugs for serious conditions that have shown encouraging early clinical results and may demonstrate substantial improvements over available medicines. Additionally, the FDA granted pemigatinib Orphan Drug designation for the treatment of cholangiocarcinoma, a designation granted to investigational compounds intended for the safe and effective treatment, diagnosis or prevention of rare diseases or disorders that affect fewer than 200,000 people.'}{'symbol': 'IBM', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'International Business Machines Corporation, AI & the Future of Work: Virtual Summit, Dec 04, 2019', 'text': 'International Business Machines Corporation, AI & The Future of Work: Virtual Summit, Dec 04, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'INTU', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Intuit Inc. Solicits Proxies from the Shareholders', 'text': 'On November 27, 2019, Intuit Inc. filed a definitive proxy statement and urged the shareholders to vote against the shareholder proposal from Hal S. Scott to adopt a mandatory arbitration bylaw in the annual meeting of shareholders to be held on January 23, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'JNPR', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Juniper Networks, Inc. Announces the Resignation of Bikash Koley as Executive Vice President, Chief Technology Officer', 'text': 'On November 22, 2019, Bikash Koley informed Juniper Networks, Inc. that he will resign as the Company’s Executive Vice President, Chief Technology Officer. Mr. Koley will remain with the Company in his current role until January 3, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'KEYS', 'date': '2019-11-27 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Keysight Technologies Reports Q4 Non-Gaap Earnings Per Share $1.33', 'text': 'KEYSIGHT TECHNOLOGIES REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.SEES Q1 2020 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.04 TO $1.10 EXCLUDING ITEMS.Q4 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.02.Q4 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.33.Q4 REVENUE $1.122 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.09 BILLION.SEES Q1 2020 REVENUE $1.045 BILLION TO $1.065 BILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.18 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'LHX', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'L3Harris Technologies, Inc. Closes Its Issuance and Sale of $400,000,000 Aggregate Principal Amount of Its 2.900% Notes Due 2029', 'text': 'On November 27, 2019, L3Harris Technologies, Inc. closed its issuance and sale of $400,000,000 aggregate principal amount of its 2.900% Notes due 2029 (the “Notes”). The Notes were offered and sold under L3Harris’ “automatic shelf” Registration Statement on Form S-3 (Registration No. 333-233827) filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission (“SEC”) on September 18, 2019 (the “Registration Statement”). In connection with the issuance and sale of the Notes, L3Harris filed a Prospectus, dated September 18, 2019, and a related Prospectus Supplement, dated November 13, 2019, which relate to the issuance and sale of the Notes, and entered into an Underwriting Agreement, dated as of November 13, 2019, with BofA Securities, Inc., Citigroup Global Markets Inc. and Wells Fargo Securities, LLC, on behalf of themselves and the several underwriters named therein, which was filed as an exhibit to L3Harris’ Current Report on Form 8-K filed with the SEC on November 14, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'MKC', 'date': '2019-11-27 20:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'McCormick Announces Increase In Quarterly Dividend', 'text': 'MCCORMICK ANNOUNCES INCREASE IN QUARTERLY DIVIDEND.SETS QUARTERLY DIVIDEND OF $0.62PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'MCK', 'date': '2019-11-27 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': "McKesson Says To Co's Knowledge, There Have Been No Additional Developments Beyond Disclosure Of Receiving A Subpoena In Most Recent 10-Q", 'text': 'MCKESSON, IN RESPONSE TO REPORT ON PROBE OF OPIOID MAKERS, DISTRIBUTORS, SAYS INFORMATION ABOUT CO GETTING A SUBPOENA WAS DISCLOSED IN MOST RECENT 10-Q.MCKESSON SAYS "TO OUR KNOWLEDGE, THERE HAVE BEEN NO ADDITIONAL DEVELOPMENTS" BEYOND CO\'S DISCLOSURE OF RECEIVING A SUBPOENA IN CO\'S MOST RECENT 10-Q.'}{'symbol': 'NEM', 'date': '2019-11-27 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Kore Mining Announces Agreement With Newmont Goldcorp', 'text': 'KORE MINING LTD - ANNOUNCES AGREEMENT WITH NEWMONT GOLDCORP.KORE MINING - NEWMONT GOLDCORP AGREED TO ACCEPT SHARES IN SETTLEMENT OF FUTURE $1 MILLION PAYMENT ON ANNOUNCING OF ASSESSMENT FOR IMPERIAL GOLD PROJECT.KORE MINING - AMENDMENT DOES NOT OBLIGATE CO TO COMPLETE ECONOMIC ASSESSMENT WITHIN NEXT 12 MONTHS; OTHER PROVISIONS OF AGREEMENT REMAIN IN FULL FORCE.'}{'symbol': 'NEM', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Outcrop Gold Corp. and Newmont Goldcorp Corporation Resumes Exploration on the Lyra Project', 'text': 'Outcrop Gold Corp. announced that the company and its funding partner Newmont Goldcorp will resume exploration on the Lyra Project after a lifting of a condition of Force Majeure related to security. Outcrop Gold believes that Lyra captures what the Company refers to as the "Buritica Trend" which is a 30km extension of the Tonusco Fault system that bisects the primary Buritica vein system and continues to the south to ANZA. The Company thinks that the Tonusco Fault is the source of the gold and base metal-bearing fluids that formed the Buritica veins in second order dilational zones that spay off the Tonusco. Lyra provides a large strategically located piece of ground between Continental Gold\'s Buritica and Orosur Mining\'s ANZA projects. Newmont made a large strategic investment in Continental Gold and actively funds ANZA exploration under an agreement with Orosur Mining. The Company believes that Lyra provides Newmont Goldcorp and Outcrop a strategically important gold trend to explore. The Lyra Project has a high potential to host high-grade Carbonate Base Metal Gold (CBM(Au)) vein systems like Buritica. Existing stream sediment anomalies on Lyra resemble stream sediment anomalies associated with both Buritica and ANZA. The Tonusco Fault "connects" Buritica and ANZA, probably as a first order control of mineralization in this part of the Middle. Very limited prospecting produced a sample of 0.6m at 70 g Au/t from a quartz-sulfide vein in a caved historic working in the very northeast of the Lyra project closest to Buritica. Only four channel samples of vein and a tailings sample from an active artisan were taken. The samples ranged from low of 14.75 g Au/t to a high of 70 g Au/t with a median grade of 17.5 g Au/t and a mean grade of 32.5 g Au/t. High-grade samples this close to Buritica are especially encouraging. The Lyra Project is in Antioquia department, 120 km northwest of Medellin and a two-hour drive from the city. The Lyra project consists of 14 concession contract applications totaling 54,895 hectares covering 30km of the Tonusco Fault that extends south from the Buritica vein system. The Buritica vein system is located adjacent to the Tonusco fault and is interpreted to be controlled by a pre-existing Cretaceous-aged fault system which has been reactivated by a Miocene-aged east-northeast-west-southwest fault system. The Miocene-aged structures control the emplacement of an intrusive complex which is associated with the vein system. A second prospective regional fault structure, the Mistratos 10km to the West.'}{'symbol': 'PRU', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Robbins Geller Rudman & Dowd LLP Files Class Action Suit Against Prudential Financial, Inc', 'text': 'Robbins Geller Rudman & Dowd LLP announced that it filed a class action on behalf of an institutional investor seeking to represent purchasers of Prudential Financial, Inc. common stock during the period between February 15, 2019 and August 2, 2019 (the “Class Period”). This action was filed in the District of New Jersey and is captioned City of Warren Police and Fire Ret. Sys. v. Prudential Financial, Inc., et al., No. 19-cv-20839. The Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995 permits any investor who purchased Prudential common stock during the Class Period to seek appointment as lead plaintiff in the Prudential class action lawsuit. A lead plaintiff acts on behalf of all other class members in directing the Prudential class action lawsuit. The lead plaintiff can select a law firm of its choice to litigate the Prudential class action lawsuit. An investor’s ability to share in any potential future recovery of the Prudential class action lawsuit is not dependent upon serving as lead plaintiff.'}{'symbol': 'NOW', 'date': '2019-11-27 21:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ServiceNow CEO William Mcdermott Reports Open Market Purchase Of 3,600 Shares On Nov 25', 'text': 'SERVICENOW SAYS CEO WILLIAM MCDERMOTT REPORTS OPEN MARKET PURCHASE OF 3,600 SHARES AT AVERAGE PRICE OF $278.93PER SHARE ON NOV 25 - SEC FILING.'}{'symbol': 'TSLA', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Tesla CEO Musk Tweets "250K", Indicating Co Received 250,000 Cybertruck Orders So Far - Tweet', 'text': 'Nov 26  - :TESLA CEO ELON MUSK TWEETS "250K", INDICATING CO RECEIVED 250,000 CYBERTRUCK ORDERS SO FAR - TWEET.'}{'symbol': 'ULTA', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ulta Beauty, Inc. Appoints Patricia Little to its Board of Directors', 'text': 'Ulta Beauty, Inc. announced that Patricia Little, former Senior Vice President and Chief Financial Officer of The Hershey Company has been appointed to its Board of Directors effective November 27, 2019. Ms. Little joins the Ulta Beauty board with more than 30 years of professional financial and leadership experience. Patricia retired from her role as Senior Vice President and Chief Financial Officer of The Hershey Company in 2019. Prior to joining Hershey, Patricia was the Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer at Kelly Services, Inc. and spent 24 years with Ford Motor Company holding a variety of leadership roles. Ms. Little holds a B.S. from Drake University and an MBA from Carnegie Mellon University. Ms. Little currently serves as a member of the Board of Directors of McCormick & Company, Inc. and is the chair of its Audit Committee.'}{'symbol': 'USB', 'date': '2019-11-27 14:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'U.S. Bancorp - On Nov 27, Co Issued €175 Mln Aggregate Principal Amount Of 0.850% Medium-Term Notes', 'text': 'U.S. BANCORP - ON NOV 27, CO ISSUED €175 MILLION AGGREGATE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT OF 0.850% MEDIUM-TERM NOTES, SERIES X (SENIOR), DUE JUNE 7, 2024 - SEC FILING.'}{'symbol': 'WRB', 'date': '2019-11-27 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'W. R. Berkley Corporation(NYSE:WRB) added to S&P 500 EQUAL WEIGHTED', 'text': 'W. R. Berkley Corporation(NYSE:WRB) added to S&P 500 EQUAL WEIGHTED'}{'symbol': 'YUM', 'date': '2019-11-27 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'KFC Canada Introduces Plant-Based Fried Chicken', 'text': 'KFC Canada: :KFC CANADA INTRODUCES PLANT'}